 "about_text": "YUKI-SIS is a contemporary art gallery in Tokyo's Nihombashi Kayabacho district, currently directed by Yuki Terajima. The gallery's name blends the director's own name with the Egyptian goddess Isis. Before settling in Kayabacho in 2023, the gallery operated in other Tokyo neighborhoods linked by the word \"bridge\" (hashi), including Asakusabashi and near Nihombashi Mitsukoshimae. Its current space, on the second floor of the Koura Dai-Ichi Building overlooking a river and bridge leading to Tokyo Bay, sits among several other galleries in the same building. YUKI-SIS presents a program spanning painting, photography, printmaking, sculpture, and animation, and participates in art fairs such as Art Fair Tokyo.",
